# World 2s BASE ocean (SPEC 11, Base ocean animation): the terrain strip water, lines 208-255, where the islands and
# ships stand, in colour cycling (a swell of 64 frames, a counter-wave of 256, a breathing of 512). Ctrl+L, W, 4 starts
# mission 4 on the base pad, the chopper stays landed. Synced to the game frame (AGK frame=N prints, as tests/w2sea.agk),
# so every profile shows the same step: a = frame 288, b = frame 352. The strip water pixels are pens 1, 6, 7 and
# change colour from a to b; the old build's strip is still (this was shown red on main build: a pixel never changes).
# Pixels picked from the a500 and a1200 shots (the AGA gradient behind differs, the pens do not).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 525
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x02
wait 30
press fire 2
wait 60
wait-serial "AGK frame=288" 300
screenshot a
wait-serial "AGK frame=352" 300
screenshot b
expect-color a 8 212 0x59A
expect-color b 8 212 0x367
expect-color a 30 215 0xADE
expect-color b 30 215 0xCEE
expect-color a 124 221 0x59A
expect-color b 124 221 0x367
expect-serial "AGK start world=2 mission=4"
expect-no-serial "ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 85
expect-min-chip-free 96
